# Personal Stock Analysis Platform Roadmap

## 1. Objective

Design a personal stock analysis platform that collects data from multiple market sources, calculates technical and fundamental indicators within its own system, and converts the results into source-stamped analytical reports.

The platform will not provide investment advice or execute trades automatically.

## 2. Source and API Inventory

### 2.1 Financial Modeling Prep

Primary provider for market prices, company data, financial statements, earnings calendars, and news.

Base URL:

```text
https://financialmodelingprep.com
```

Required endpoints:

```text
GET /stable/quote?symbol=AAPL
GET /stable/historical-price-eod/full?symbol=AAPL
GET /stable/profile?symbol=AAPL
GET /stable/income-statement?symbol=AAPL
GET /stable/balance-sheet-statement?symbol=AAPL
GET /stable/cash-flow-statement?symbol=AAPL
GET /stable/earnings?symbol=AAPL
GET /stable/earnings-calendar
GET /stable/news/stock?symbols=AAPL
GET /stable/news/stock-latest?page=0&limit=20
```

Intended uses:

- OHLCV and current prices
- Raw data for technical indicators
- Company profiles
- Financial statements
- Earnings dates
- Earnings expectations
- Company news
- Index and sector ETF data

The API key must never be exposed to the client. Whenever supported, it should be sent in an HTTP header rather than included in the URL.

An individual plan may be used while the application remains personal. If the application is later opened to other users, data display and redistribution licensing must be reassessed.

### 2.2 FRED

Provider of macroeconomic data.

Primary endpoint:

```text
GET https://api.stlouisfed.org/fred/series/observations
```

Initial series:

- `DGS2`: 2-year US Treasury yield
- `DGS10`: 10-year US Treasury yield
- `DFII10`: 10-year real interest rate
- `T10Y2`: 10Y–2Y yield spread
- `T10Y3M`: 10Y–3M yield spread
- `SOFR`: Secured Overnight Financing Rate
- `FEDFUNDS`: Federal funds rate
- `CPIAUCSL`: Consumer Price Index
- `CPILFESL`: Core Consumer Price Index
- `UNRATE`: Unemployment rate
- `PAYEMS`: Nonfarm payroll employment
- `WALCL`: Federal Reserve balance sheet
- `RRPONTSYD`: Overnight reverse repurchase agreements
- `BAMLH0A0HYM2`: High-yield corporate bond spread
- `DCOILWTICO`: WTI crude oil price

Source restrictions and copyright notes must be recorded for every series.

### 2.3 SEC EDGAR

Official source for company filings and financial-data verification.

Required endpoints:

```text
GET https://data.sec.gov/submissions/CIK##########.json
GET https://data.sec.gov/api/xbrl/companyfacts/CIK##########.json
GET https://data.sec.gov/api/xbrl/frames/us-gaap/{concept}/{unit}/{period}.json
```

Bulk data:

```text
https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/daily-index/xbrl/companyfacts.zip
```

Intended uses:

- Company filing history
- Revenue, earnings, cash flow, and balance-sheet items
- Independent verification of FMP data
- Latest report and filing dates
- Financial growth calculations

SEC access policies, rate limits, and identifying `User-Agent` requirements must be followed.

### 2.4 CFTC

Source for Commitments of Traders and futures-market positioning data.

Initial dataset:

```text
Legacy_All
Dataset ID: srt6-5q2f
```

JSON access:

```text
GET https://publicreporting.cftc.gov/resource/srt6-5q2f.json
```

Because the dataset contains both Futures Only and Futures and Options Combined records, report-type filtering will be mandatory.

COT Index calculation:

```text
100 × (current net position − 156-week minimum)
    / (156-week maximum − 156-week minimum)
```

### 2.5 Unusual Whales

Provider of options, gamma, and dark-pool data.

Base URL and authentication:

```text
https://api.unusualwhales.com
Authorization: Bearer API_KEY
```

Required endpoints:

```text
GET /api/market/market-tide
GET /api/market/oi-change
GET /api/stock/{ticker}/gex-levels
GET /api/stock/{ticker}/iv-rank
GET /api/stock/{ticker}/max-pain
GET /api/stock/{ticker}/oi-change
GET /api/stock/{ticker}/options-volume
GET /api/darkpool/recent
```

Intended uses:

- Net call and put premium
- Call and put volume
- Open-interest changes
- Gamma flip
- Call and put walls
- Gamma magnet
- IV Rank
- Max Pain
- Dark-pool transactions
- Market Tide

Personal and professional usage rules must be treated separately. The data will not be redistributed to other users.

## 3. Unified Data Layer

Data from every provider will be normalized into a shared format containing:

- Symbol
- Source
- Observation timestamp
- Retrieval timestamp
- Freshness status
- Raw value
- Adjusted value
- Currency
- Data-quality score
- Verification result
- API endpoint version
- Source licensing category

Missing or stale values will never be filled with invented estimates. Values will be labelled as “last known,” “stale,” or “unverified.”

## 4. Technical Analysis Engine

The following indicators will be calculated from raw OHLCV data:

- EMA 9, 21, and 50
- SMA 20, 50, and 200
- RSI 14
- ATR
- MACD
- ADX
- Relative volume
- Bollinger Band width
- Relative strength versus SPY
- Relative strength versus the relevant sector ETF
- Fibonacci levels
- Swing highs and lows
- Support and resistance zones
- Chandelier exit line
- Daily and weekly trends

Whenever possible, indicators will be calculated internally from raw data rather than taken directly from a provider.

## 5. Stock X-Ray Model

Structure-score components:

- Trend alignment: 30 points
- Relative strength versus SPY: 20 points
- Relative volume: 15 points
- Support and resistance quality: 20 points
- Compression and range structure: 15 points

The structure score and data-quality score will be displayed separately. A high score will not imply that the price is guaranteed to rise.

## 6. Trend and Exit Plan

The trend score will evaluate:

- Price position relative to moving averages
- Moving-average alignment
- Moving-average slopes
- Pullback support
- Structural damage
- Volume confirmation
- Relative market strength
- Sector and weekly-chart alignment

The exit line will be selected from EMA9, EMA21, SMA50, Chandelier, rising lows, or the latest swing low according to the investment horizon and volatility.

## 7. Pre-Earnings Model

Model components:

- Implied move versus historical movement: 20%
- Options premium direction: 35%
- Open-interest changes: 10%
- Gamma exposure: 5%
- Dark-pool direction: 10%
- Historical earnings performance: 20%

Additional context:

- Analyst expectations
- Previous management commentary
- Revenue and earnings growth
- Recent news
- Sector comparisons

The result will be presented through bearish, base, and bullish scenarios rather than as a definitive directional call.

## 8. Macro and Risk Dashboard

The dashboard will include:

- Market indexes
- Treasury yields
- US Dollar Index
- Gold and oil
- VIX, VXN, and MOVE
- VIX term structure
- Market breadth
- Sector rotation
- COT positioning
- Options gamma regime
- Upcoming economic events

Every card will display its source, observation date, and freshness status.

## 9. Report-Generation Pipeline

1. Retrieve raw data.
2. Store the source response in an encrypted cache.
3. Validate and normalize the data.
4. Calculate technical indicators.
5. Generate deterministic scores.
6. Attach source and freshness metadata.
7. Send only sanitized results to the language model.
8. Generate the explanatory report.
9. Revalidate every number in the narrative against the source data.
10. Save the report as an immutable version.
11. Measure performance automatically when the evaluation horizon matures.

The language model will not generate numbers or scores. It will only explain previously calculated results.

## 10. Model Track Record

Every analysis will record:

- Analysis timestamp
- Data version
- Scores
- Scenario levels
- Forecast horizon
- Results after 5, 21, and 63 trading days
- Range accuracy
- Directional accuracy
- Maximum favourable and adverse movement
- Model and rule version

Failed analyses will not be deleted. Performance percentages will not be shown when the sample size is insufficient.

## 11. Privacy

- Only necessary portfolio data will be stored.
- Names, email addresses, and brokerage account numbers will not be collected.
- Identity or account information will not be sent to the language model.
- User data will not be used for model training.
- Deletion must cover portfolio data, analyses, conversations, and backups.
- Sensitive information will be removed from logs.

## 12. Cybersecurity

- API keys will never be exposed to the client.
- Keys will be stored in the operating system’s secure credential vault.
- Keys will not be shared through chat.
- The database, cache, and backups will be encrypted.
- Outbound connections will be restricted to an approved provider list.
- Inputs will be validated.
- Request-rate and spending limits will be enforced.
- External API responses will be treated as untrusted data and validated.
- Dependencies, source code, and repositories will be scanned for vulnerabilities and exposed secrets.
- The application will be inaccessible from the public internet by default.
- The first version will not be able to submit brokerage orders.
- Model output will never directly execute code, database queries, or trading instructions.

## 13. API Access Sequence

### Phase 1 — Free Official Sources

- Create a FRED account and API key.
- Establish the SEC EDGAR connection.
- Establish the CFTC COT connection.

Completion criterion: macroeconomic, financial, and COT data can be retrieved with source metadata.

### Phase 2 — FMP Prototype

- Create a personal FMP account.
- Retrieve prices and OHLCV.
- Retrieve financial statements.
- Retrieve the earnings calendar.
- Retrieve company news.

Completion criterion: all raw data required for the Stock X-Ray and Trend models is available.

### Phase 3 — Technical Engine

- Calculate indicators.
- Generate scores.
- Detect support and resistance.
- Select exit lines.
- Implement the data-quality system.

Completion criterion: identical input always produces an identical result.

### Phase 4 — Unusual Whales

- Market Tide
- GEX
- IV Rank
- Max Pain
- Open-interest changes
- Options volume
- Dark-pool activity

Completion criterion: all required data for options and pre-earnings models is available.

### Phase 5 — Reporting and Track Record

- Report templates
- Source metadata
- Model explanations
- Automated outcome measurement

Completion criterion: every report’s data, source, rule version, and subsequent performance can be traced.

### Phase 6 — Security Verification

- Threat model
- Key management
- Encryption
- Log sanitization
- Backup and restoration
- Security testing

Completion criterion: sensitive information is absent from client code, logs, and model inputs.

## 14. Out of Scope

- Automated trade execution
- Guaranteed returns or definitive directional predictions
- Unlicensed data redistribution
- Copying reports from another platform
- Unexplainable AI-generated scores
- Sharing user data without the user’s knowledge

